.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pepe-api 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-api \- Load\-test every endpoint of an OpenAPI spec
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe api\fR [\fB\-\-auth\fR] [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-writes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISPEC\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Load\-test every endpoint of an OpenAPI spec
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\fR \fI<AUTH>\fR
Credentials: bearer:TOKEN, basic:USER:PASSWORD, apikey:VALUE, header:NAME=VALUE or query:NAME=VALUE
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Base URL to send requests to, instead of the spec\*(Aqs server
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Run every endpoint that has the values it needs. Without \-\-all, \-\-tag or \-\-only, nothing runs until it\*(Aqs picked on the plan screen
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Run the endpoints with this tag, e.g. \-\-tag Billing
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<ONLY>\fR
Run the endpoints matching this, e.g. \*(AqGET /pets*\*(Aq or \*(Aq/pets/*\*(Aq
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fI<SKIP>\fR
Leave out endpoints matching this
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<NAME=VALUE[,VALUE]>\fR
A parameter\*(Aqs value(s), rotated through: \-\-set id=1,2,3
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-writes\fR
Let \-\-all, \-\-tag and \-\-only switch on POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE too
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISPEC\fR>
The OpenAPI spec: a file or URL, JSON or YAML
